"version;-tearfree_backport-1.patch\"/>"
msgstr ""
"Remendo opcional: <ulink url=\"&patch-root;/xorg-server-&xorg-server-"
"version;-tearfree_backport-1.patch\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><bridgehead>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:91
#, xml-text
msgid "Xorg Server Dependencies"
msgstr "Dependências do Servidor Xorg"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><bridgehead>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:93
#, xml-text
msgid "Required"
msgstr "Exigidas"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:95
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<xref linkend=\"libxcvt\"/>, <xref linkend=\"pixman\"/>, <xref "
"linkend=\"xorg7-font\"/> (only font-util), and at runtime: <xref "
"role=\"runtime\" linkend=\"xkeyboard-config\"/>"
msgstr ""
"<xref linkend=\"libxcvt\"/>, <xref linkend=\"pixman\"/>, <xref "
"linkend=\"xorg7-font\"/> (somente &quot;font-util&quot;) e, ao tempo da "
"execução, <xref role=\"runtime\" linkend=\"xkeyboard-config\"/>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><bridgehead>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:101
#, xml-text
msgid "Recommended"
msgstr "Recomendadas"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:103
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<phrase revision=\"sysv\"><xref linkend='dbus'/>, <xref role=\"runtime\" "
"linkend=\"elogind\"/> (runtime; <systemitem "
"class='library'>libelogind</systemitem> also referred at build time but it's"
" not really useful),</phrase> <xref linkend=\"libepoxy\"/> (needed for "
"glamor), <xref linkend=\"libtirpc\"/>, <phrase revision=\"systemd\"><xref "
"role=\"runtime\" linkend=\"systemd\"/> (runtime),</phrase> and <xref "
"role='runtime' linkend='xorg-libinput-driver'/> (runtime)"
msgstr ""
"<phrase revision=\"sysv\"><xref linkend='dbus'/>, <xref role=\"runtime\" "
"linkend=\"elogind\"/> (tempo de execução; <systemitem "
"class='library'>libelogind</systemitem> também referenciada em tempo de "
"construção, mas realmente não é útil),</phrase> <xref linkend=\"libepoxy\"/>"
" (necessário para glamor), <xref linkend=\"libtirpc\"/>, <phrase "
"revision=\"systemd\"><xref role=\"runtime\" linkend=\"systemd\"/> (tempo de "
"execução),</phrase> e <xref role='runtime' linkend='xorg-libinput-driver'/> "
"(tempo de execução)"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:119
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Although it's possible to<phrase revision='sysv'> build this package without"
" <xref linkend='dbus'/> installed or</phrase> run the Xorg server without "
"<phrase revision='sysv'><xref linkend='elogind'/></phrase><phrase "
"revision='systemd'><xref linkend='systemd'/> (rebuilt with PAM)</phrase> "
"functioning, it would require running the Xorg server as the &root; user or "
"Xorg server will malfunction or even fail to start.  The BLFS editors "
"strongly discourage skipping <phrase revision='sysv'>these two "
"dependencies</phrase><phrase revision='systemd'>this dependency</phrase>.  "
"Do not attempt to do so unless you really know what you are doing."
msgstr ""
"Embora seja possível<phrase revision='sysv'> construir esse pacote sem <xref"
" linkend='dbus'/> instalado ou</phrase> executar o servidor Xorg sem <phrase"
" revision='sysv'><xref linkend='elogind'/></phrase><phrase "
"revision='systemd'><xref linkend='systemd'/> (reconstruído com PAM)</phrase>"
" funcionando, exigiria executar o servidor Xorg como o(a) usuário(a) &root;,"
" ou o servidor Xorg funcionará mal ou até mesmo falhará ao iniciar. Os(As) "
"editores(as) do BLFS fortemente desencorajam ignorar <phrase "
"revision='sysv'>essas duas dependências</phrase><phrase "
"revision='systemd'>essa dependência</phrase>. Não tente fazer isso a menos "
"que você realmente saiba o que está fazendo."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><bridgehead>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:134
#, xml-text
msgid "Optional"
msgstr "Opcionais"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:136
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<xref role=\"runtime\" linkend=\"acpid\"/> (runtime), <xref "
"linkend=\"doxygen\"/> (to build API documentation), <xref linkend=\"fop\"/> "
"(to build documentation), <xref linkend=\"libunwind\"/>, <xref "
"linkend=\"nettle\"/>, <xref linkend=\"libgcrypt\"/>, <xref linkend=\"xcb-"
"utilities\"/> (to build Xephyr), <xref linkend=\"xmlto\"/> (to build "
"documentation), <xref linkend=\"xkeyboard-config\"/> (for tests), <ulink "
"url=\"https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/xorg/test/rendercheck\">rendercheck</ulink>"
" (for tests), and <ulink "
"url=\"https://www.x.org/archive/individual/doc/\">xorg-sgml-doctools</ulink>"
" (to build documentation)"
msgstr ""
"<xref role=\"runtime\" linkend=\"acpid\"/> (tempo de execução), <xref "
"linkend=\"doxygen\"/> (para construir documentação da API), <xref "
"linkend=\"fop\"/> (para construir documentação), <xref "
"linkend=\"libunwind\"/>, <xref linkend=\"nettle\"/>, <xref "
"linkend=\"libgcrypt\"/>, <xref linkend=\"xcb-utilities\"/> (para construir "
"Xephyr), <xref linkend=\"xmlto\"/> (para construir documentação), <xref "
"linkend=\"xkeyboard-config\"/> (para testes), <ulink "
"url=\"https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/xorg/test/rendercheck\">rendercheck</ulink>"
" (para testes) e <ulink "
"url=\"https://www.x.org/archive/individual/doc/\">xorg-sgml-doctools</ulink>"
" (para construir documentação)"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:151
#, xml-text
msgid "Kernel Configuration"
msgstr "Configuração do Núcleo"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:154
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The traditional Device Dependent X (DDX) drivers have been removed from BLFS"
" in favor of the &modesetting_drv; driver which will be built as a part of "
"this package.  To use the &modesetting_drv; driver, the kernel must provide "
"a Direct Rendering Manager (DRM) driver for your GPU."
msgstr ""
"Os controladores tradicionais Device Dependent X (DDX) foram removidos do "
"BLFS em favor do controlador &modesetting_drv; que será construído como "
"parte desse pacote. Para usar o controlador &modesetting_drv;, o núcleo "
"precisa fornecer um controlador Direct Rendering Manager (DRM) para a tua "
"GPU."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:162
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If your GPU supports 3D acceleration and <xref linkend='mesa'/> provides a "
"Gallium3D driver for utilizing its 3D capability, you should have already "
"enabled the necessary kernel configuration options in <xref linkend='mesa-"
"kernel'/>.  Otherwise, you need to find the kernel configuration option of "
"the DRM driver for the GPU and enable it.  Notably, the virtual GPUs "
"provided by some virtual machine managers:"
msgstr ""
"Se a tua GPU suporta aceleração 3D e <xref linkend='mesa'/> fornece um "
"controlador Gallium3D para utilizar a capacidade 3D dele, você já deveria "
"ter habilitado as necessárias opções de configuração de núcleo em <xref "
"linkend='mesa-kernel'/>. Caso contrário, você precisa encontrar a opção de "
"configuração do núcleo do controlador DRM para a GPU e habilitá-la. "
"Notavelmente, as GPUs virtuais fornecidas por alguns gerenciadores de "
"máquinas virtuais:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:175
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If the kernel does not provide a DRM driver for your GPU, on most x86 "
"systems the <quote>simple frame buffer</quote> DRM driver running on VESA or"
" UEFI frame buffer can be used as a fallback.  Enable the following options "
"in the kernel configurations if you don't have a dedicated DRM driver for "
"the GPU, or you want to keep the simple frame buffer driver as a fallback in"
" case the dedicated driver fails:"
msgstr ""
"Se o núcleo não fornecer um controlador DRM para a tua GPU, na maioria dos "
"sistemas x86 o controlador DRM <quote>simple frame buffer</quote> executando"
" em VESA ou UEFI frame buffer pode ser usado como substituto. Habilite as "
"seguintes opções nas configurações do núcleo, se você não tiver um "
"controlador DRM dedicado para a GPU ou quiser manter o controlador simple "
"frame buffer como um substituto caso o controlador dedicado falhe:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:187
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To allow the kernel to print debug messages at an early boot stage, "
"<option>CONFIG_DRM</option> and <option>CONFIG_DRM_SIMPLEDRM</option> should"
" not be built as kernel modules unless an initramfs will be used."
msgstr ""
"Para permitir que o núcleo imprima mensagens de depuração em um estágio "
"inicial da inicialização, <option>CONFIG_DRM</option> e "
"<option>CONFIG_DRM_SIMPLEDRM</option> não deveriam ser construídos como "
"módulos do núcleo, a menos que um initramfs seja usado."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:194
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you want to use the simple frame buffer driver on a system booted via "
"BIOS (instead of UEFI), add the following line before the first "
"<literal>menuentry</literal> block in the "
"<filename>/boot/grub/grub.cfg</filename> file to initialize the VESA frame "
"buffer:"
msgstr ""
"Se você quiser usar o controlador simple frame buffer em um sistema "
"inicializado via BIOS (em vez de UEFI), adicione a seguinte linha antes do "
"primeiro bloco <literal>menuentry</literal> no arquivo "
"<filename>/boot/grub/grub. cfg</filename> para inicializar o VESA frame "
"buffer:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:201
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<literal>set gfxpayload=<replaceable>1024x768x32</replaceable></literal>"
msgstr ""
"<literal>set gfxpayload=<replaceable>1024x768x32</replaceable></literal>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:204
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"You may replace <literal>1024</literal>, <literal>768</literal>, and "
"<literal>32</literal> with a resolution and color depth setting suitable for"
" your monitor."
msgstr ""
"Você pode substituir <literal>1024</literal>, <literal>768</literal> e "
"<literal>32</literal> por uma configuração de resolução e profundidade de "
"cor adequada ao teu monitor."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:210
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If all of these DRM drivers do not work for you and you need to use a DDX "
"driver with a non-DRM kernel GPU driver (usually named "
"<option>CONFIG_FB_*</option> in the kernel configuration, or existing as "
"out-tree kernel modules), or you need an device specific functionality "
"requiring a DDX driver, consult <ulink url=\"&BLFS113;\">a prior version of "
"BLFS</ulink>, or <ulink url=\"&BLFS76;\">an even earlier prior "
"version</ulink> for more DDX drivers."
msgstr ""
"Se todos esses controladores DRM não funcionarem para você e você precisar "
"usar um controlador DDX com um controlador de GPU de núcleo não DRM "
"(geralmente chamado de <option>CONFIG_FB_*</option> na configuração do "
"núcleo, ou existente como módulos do núcleo fora da árvore) ou você precisar"
" de uma funcionalidade específica do dispositivo que exige um controlador "
"DDX, consulte <ulink url=\"&BLFS113;\">uma versão anterior do BLFS</ulink> "
"ou <ulink url=\"&BLFS76;\">uma versão ainda mais anterior</ulink> para mais "
"controladores DDX."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:226
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of Xorg Server"
msgstr "Instalação do Servidor Xorg"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:229
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"First, if you need the TearFree option to work around screen tearing, apply "
"the backported patch:"
msgstr ""
"Primeiro, se você precisar da opção TearFree para contornar o rasgo de tela,"
" aplique o remendo reimplementado:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:233
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput remap=\"pre\">patch -Np1 -i ../xorg-server-&xorg-server-"
"version;-tearfree_backport-1.patch</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput remap=\"pre\">patch -Np1 -i ../xorg-server-&xorg-server-"
"version;-tearfree_backport-1.patch</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:236
#, xml-text
msgid "Install the server by running the following commands:"
msgstr "Instale o servidor executando os seguintes comandos:"

#.  To editors: Ironically -D systemd_logind=true shows up only for
#.          **sysv** revision.  No it's not a bug.  It's used to make the
#.          building system error out when dbus is not installed and emphasis
#.          that we don't support a configuration lacking a recommended
#.          dependency.  On systemd dbus is installed in LFS.  Despite the
#.          naming, it controls elogind support as well.
#.          It's harmless to have this option for systemd revision as well
#.          but I cannot figure out how to write it up in the Explanations
#.          section for systemd revision, so just omit it for systemd
#.          revision.
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:251
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup ..               \\\n"
"      --prefix=$XORG_PREFIX  \\\n"
"      --localstatedir=/var   \\\n"
"      -D glamor=true         \\\n"
"      -D systemd_logind=true \\\n"
"      -D xkb_output_dir=/var/lib/xkb &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup ..               \\\n"
"      --prefix=$XORG_PREFIX  \\\n"
"      --localstatedir=/var   \\\n"
"      -D glamor=true         \\\n"
"      -D systemd_logind=true \\\n"
"      -D xkb_output_dir=/var/lib/xkb &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:262
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup ..              \\\n"
"      --prefix=$XORG_PREFIX \\\n"
"      --localstatedir=/var  \\\n"
"      -D glamor=true        \\\n"
"      -D xkb_output_dir=/var/lib/xkb &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup ..              \\\n"
"      --prefix=$XORG_PREFIX \\\n"
"      --localstatedir=/var  \\\n"
"      -D glamor=true        \\\n"
"      -D xkb_output_dir=/var/lib/xkb &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:273
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To test the results, issue: <command>ninja test</command>. You will need to "
"run <command>ldconfig</command> as the <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user first or some tests may fail."
msgstr ""
"Para testar os resultados, emita: &quot;<command>ninja test</command>&quot;."
" Você precisará executar &quot;<command>ldconfig</command>&quot; como o(a) "
"usuário(a) &quot;<systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>&quot; "
"primeiro ou alguns testes possivelmente falhem."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:279
#, xml-text
msgid "Now as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Agora como o(a) usuário(a) &quot;<systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>&quot;:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/x/installing/xorg-server.xml:283
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>ninja install &amp;&amp;\n"
"mkdir -pv /etc/X11/xorg.conf.d &amp;&amp;\n"
"install -v -d -m1777 /tmp/.{ICE,X11}-unix &amp;&amp;\n"
"cat &gt;&gt; /etc/sysconfig/createfiles &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal>/tmp/.ICE-unix dir 1777 root root\n"
"/tmp/.X11-unix dir 1777 root root</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>ninja install &amp;&amp;\n"
"mkdir -pv /etc/X11/xorg.conf.d &amp;&amp;\n"
"install -v -d -m1777 /tmp/.{ICE,X11}-unix &amp;&amp;\n"
"cat &gt;&gt; /etc/sysconfig/createfiles &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal>/tmp/.ICE-unix dir 1777 root root\n"
"/tmp/.X11-unix dir 1777 root root</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

